        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T02:18:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not fully convinced about the benefit of creating a separate module type for this functionality. Even with `dep_api_srcs` property, the main functionality of the module, which is taking the API file(s) as input, and outputting compiled stub jar file does not change. The only difference the property introduces is how the jar file is created, which I believe can be left agnostic, rather than creating a new module type.\n\n`static_libs` (which is merge-zipped after jar file generation) and will serve the same role with and without `dep_api_srcs` defined, although `libs` property will not take any effect when `dep_api_srcs` is passed.",
      "parentUuid": "ba6500c9_f20c86c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "f1adf06b762c1da4fecd1a435a8c752313ce438e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
