      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T03:09:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The UX I was thinking of was\n```\njava_api_library_fragment { # something like this\n  name: \"framework-foo\",\n  api_files: [\n     \"current.txt\",\n  ],\n  full_surface: \"android_public_stubs.from-text\",\n}\n\njava_api_library {\n  name: \"android_public_stubs.from-text\",\n  api_files: [\u003call_files.txt\"],\n}\n```\n\nWhen computing the files for framework-foo that need to be subtracted, we can remove the api files of framework-foo from the full api_files contained in android_public_stubs.from-text (as an example). And the source input to this metalava invocation will be the stub.jar file.\n\nI think the other option (the better one imo long term) is to create something like a `passthrough-api` in metalava which does the opposite of what `--subtract-api` does.",
      "parentUuid": "fe038fc7_1a7f2b1d",
